#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:1
msgid "Release 1.8 (2014-12-14)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:3
msgid ""
"Breaking change: to address a race condition, the remote build hook "
"mechanism now uses `nix-store         --serve` on the remote machine. This "
"requires build slaves to be updated to Nix 1.8."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:8
msgid ""
"Nix now uses HTTPS instead of HTTP to access the default binary cache, "
"`cache.nixos.org`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:11
msgid ""
"`nix-env` selectors are now regular expressions. For instance, you can do"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:16
msgid "to query all packages with a name containing `zip`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:18
msgid ""
"`nix-store --read-log` can now fetch remote build logs. If a build log is "
"not available locally, then ‘nix-store -l’ will now try to download it from "
"the servers listed in the ‘log-servers’ option in nix.conf. For instance, if "
"you have the configuration option"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:23
msgid ""
"    log-servers = http://hydra.nixos.org/log\n"
"    "
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:25
msgid ""
"then it will try to get logs from `http://hydra.nixos.org/log/base name of "
"the store path`. This allows you to do things like:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:31
msgid "and get a log even if `xterm` wasn't built locally."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:33
msgid ""
"New builtin functions: `attrValues`, `deepSeq`, `fromJSON`, `readDir`, `seq`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:36
msgid ""
"`nix-instantiate --eval` now has a `--json` flag to print the resulting "
"value in JSON format."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:39
msgid ""
"`nix-copy-closure` now uses `nix-store --serve` on the remote side to send "
"or receive closures. This fixes a race condition between `nix-copy-closure` "
"and the garbage collector."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:43
msgid ""
"Derivations can specify the new special attribute `allowedRequisites`, which "
"has a similar meaning to `allowedReferences`. But instead of only enforcing "
"to explicitly specify the immediate references, it requires the derivation "
"to specify all the dependencies recursively (hence the name, requisites) "
"that are used by the resulting output."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:50
msgid ""
"On Mac OS X, Nix now handles case collisions when importing closures from "
"case-sensitive file systems. This is mostly useful for running NixOps on Mac "
"OS X."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:54
msgid ""
"The Nix daemon has new configuration options `allowed-users` (specifying the "
"users and groups that are allowed to connect to the daemon) and `trusted-"
"users` (specifying the users and groups that can perform privileged "
"operations like specifying untrusted binary caches)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:60
msgid ""
"The configuration option `build-cores` now defaults to the number of "
"available CPU cores."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:63
msgid ""
"Build users are now used by default when Nix is invoked as root. This "
"prevents builds from accidentally running as root."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:66
msgid "Nix now includes systemd units and Upstart jobs."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:68
msgid "Speed improvements to `nix-store         --optimise`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:71
msgid ""
"Language change: the `==` operator now ignores string contexts (the "
"“dependencies” of a string)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:74
msgid ""
"Nix now filters out Nix-specific ANSI escape sequences on standard error. "
"They are supposed to be invisible, but some terminals show them anyway."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:78
msgid ""
"Various commands now automatically pipe their output into the pager as "
"specified by the `PAGER` environment variable."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:81
msgid "Several improvements to reduce memory consumption in the evaluator."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-1.8.md:83
msgid ""
"This release has contributions from Adam Szkoda, Aristid Breitkreuz, Bob van "
"der Linden, Charles Strahan, darealshinji, Eelco Dolstra, Gergely Risko, "
"Joel Taylor, Ludovic Courtès, Marko Durkovic, Mikey Ariel, Paul Colomiets, "
"Ricardo M. Correia, Ricky Elrod, Robert Helgesson, Rob Vermaas, Russell "
"O'Connor, Shea Levy, Shell Turner, Sönke Hahn, Steve Purcell, Vladimír Čunát "
"and Wout Mertens."
msgstr ""
